.TH EUCLID-CLI-EMM-START-MODULE 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-emm-start-module \- let a stopped euclid module run again
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B emm start-module
.BR \-\-module " " \fIMODULE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Clears what
.BR euclid-cli-emm-stop-module (1)
recorded, so the manager runs the module again.
.PP
Its instances are started on the manager's next reconcile tick, within a
few seconds, back up to the module's minimum instance count \- the same
number a manager start would bring up. From then on the module is
ordinary again: the autoscaler grows and shrinks its pool under load,
crashed instances are restarted, and a manager restart starts it with
everything else.
.PP
Starting a module that was never stopped changes nothing and is not an
error, so this is safe to run without checking first.
.PP
This is only about the stopped state. A module that is down for another
reason \- inactive in
.IR euclid.json ,
crashing on startup, exceeding its restart limit \- is not brought back
by this;
.BR euclid-cli-emm-list-modules (1)
shows which of those it is.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-module " " \fIMODULE\fR
Module to start again, e.g. \fIftp\fR. Required. Must be a module the
manager knows about \- an unknown name is rejected with
.I "HTTP 404"
rather than silently recorded.
.SH OUTPUT
The JSON response is printed to standard output:
.RS
.TP
.I name
The module that was started.
.TP
.I stopped
.I false
\- what is now recorded for it.
.TP
.I runningInstances
How many instances the pool held when the request was answered, which
for a module that was stopped is the number of slots waiting to be
filled rather than the number running.
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The module is recorded as running again.
.TP
.B 1
The stored session is missing or not an administrator's, the module is
unknown or not a euclid module, the request could not be sent, or the
server rejected it. Details are printed to standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Bring the FTP transfer front end back:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 emm start-module --module ftp
.fi
.RE
.PP
Watch it come up:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 emm list-modules
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-emm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emm-stop-module (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emm-list-modules (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1)
